         text="Babur finds Agra's plain hot, dusty and joyless, but crosses the Yamuna to dig a great well, then a tank, a bath and orderly beds and channels. His nobles copy him along the bank, and the locals, Babur writes, call the east bank 'Kabul'. These are the first Mughal gardens in India.",
